   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re on Route 4 — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center; tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. From here: SOUTH → Route 3 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; EAST → Cerulean City — a Mart, a Pokémon Center. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: an unfamiliar area; an unfamiliar area; Route 2. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. Heads up: you have ZERO Poké Balls — you literally can\'t catch a teammate until you buy some at a Mart, so a Mart run has to come before any catching.. You just went down to the wild zubat (poison/flying-type around here) at Mt. Moon B1F — bit of bad luck. Shake it off; maybe heal up or pick your fights a little better. Your call.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 2 of 8 — next is Misty in Cerulean City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an abra around Route 24 / Route 25. It grows into my alakazam — that\'s my answer for Erika AND Koga down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "What? I\'m waiting for my friends to find me here."; "POK. BALL, and you want 1. That will be .200. Okay?"; "POK. BALL? Certainly. How many would you like?". YOUR PLAN — right now: Train the team toward ~L8 (or catch one more teammate), THEN retry. Next: Build a team strong enough to beat the wild zubat at Mt. Moon B1F, then push on toward Cerulean City. Bigger picture: Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L23), mankey (L9), spearow (L9). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "1 badge(s) earned (Boulder). Next gym: Misty of Cerulean City. Pokédex: 4 caught. She's one badge in — the adventure's really starting (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'wartortle (L23), mankey (L9), spearow (L9)', 'goal': {'short': 'Train the team toward ~L8 (or catch one more teammate), THEN retry', '